\end{tikzpicture}
\caption{Gimbal Lock Detection: The region where $|\cos(\alpha)| \leq \epsilon$ and $|\sin(\alpha)| \approx 1$ indicates gimbal lock.}
\end{figure}

\section{Error Handling}

The API implements comprehensive error handling through status codes:

\begin{itemize}
    \item \texttt{PASS}: Operation completed successfully
    \item \texttt{EUNDEFINEDBUFFER}: Null pointer detected in input/output buffers
    \item \texttt{EBUFFERTURNCATION}: Matrix dimension mismatch or non-3×3 matrix
    \item \textit{Custom}: User-defined error codes for extended validation
\end{itemize}

Error handling occurs at each phase with optional callback invocation via \texttt{on\_op\_failure}.

\section{Performance Considerations}

\subsection{Optimization Techniques}

\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Fixed Dimensions}: Use of $3 \times 3$ matrices enables unrolled matrix multiplication loops
    \item \textbf{Cache Locality}: Sequential access patterns in row-convention iteration
    \item \textbf{Callback Mechanism}: Defer non-essential operations to user-provided handlers
    \item \textbf{Early Validation}: Fail fast on invalid inputs before expensive computations
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{Memory Efficiency}

\begin{itemize}
    \item Stack-allocated temporary matrices (no dynamic allocation overhead)
    \item In-place gimbal iteration using iterator callbacks
    \item Metadata shared via pointers to avoid duplication
\end{itemize}

\section{Conclusion}

The 3D Matrix Rotation API in the Electrostatic-Sandbox framework provides a robust, efficient implementation of gimbal-based rotations with built-in gimbal lock detection. The mathematical foundation ensures correctness through orthogonal transformation properties, while the multi-phase algorithmic approach enables flexible error handling and event-driven callbacks.

Key achievements:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Constant-time performance for fixed $3 \times 3$ matrices
    \item Robust gimbal lock detection and compensation
    \item Extensible callback mechanism for custom event handling
    \item Comprehensive input validation and error reporting
\end{itemize}

The framework successfully integrates this API into distributed systems simulation, providing reliable 3D orientation transformations compliant with IEEE-1516 HLA specifications.

